From: OpenWrt
Subject: [PATCH] net: phylink: report the advertised pause request

phylink_ethtool_get_pauseparam() always reports the MLO_PAUSE_RX/TX bits of
link_config.pause. Those bits are the manual override that is only consulted
when pause autonegotiation is off; while pause AN is on the request lives in
the pause bits of link_config.advertising, which phylink seeds from the MAC's
MAC_SYM_PAUSE/MAC_ASYM_PAUSE capabilities and keeps in step with every
set_pauseparam(). Nothing seeds the override bits from that advertisement, so
until a first set_pauseparam() the two disagree and a port advertising pause
reports rx/tx off.

That is not only a wrong reading. The ethtool netlink layer pre-fills the
request from get_pauseparam(), and ethnl_set_pause() returns success without
calling set_pauseparam() when no field changed value. A port advertising pause
therefore reports off, and a request for off is discarded as a no-op with
rc 0, leaving the advertisement in place. The setting only lands if autoneg is
toggled in the same command, which restarts negotiation and drops the link.

Derive the reported rx/tx from the advertisement while pause AN is on, using
the inverse of the mapping linkmode_set_pause() applies, and keep reporting
the override bits when pause AN is off, since those are what the resolver
then enforces. get_pauseparam() becomes an exact readback of set_pauseparam()
in every combination, so the netlink change detection no longer discards a
valid request.

This changes only what is reported and, through that, which requests reach
set_pauseparam(). Capability advertisement, negotiation and MAC programming
are untouched.

---
 drivers/net/phy/phylink.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/phylink.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/phylink.c
@@ -2941,11 +2941,32 @@
 void phylink_ethtool_get_pauseparam(struct phylink *pl,
 				    struct ethtool_pauseparam *pause)
 {
+	const unsigned long *adv = pl->link_config.advertising;
+	bool rx, tx;
+
 	ASSERT_RTNL();
 
 	pause->autoneg = !!(pl->link_config.pause & MLO_PAUSE_AN);
-	pause->rx_pause = !!(pl->link_config.pause & MLO_PAUSE_RX);
-	pause->tx_pause = !!(pl->link_config.pause & MLO_PAUSE_TX);
+
+	if (pause->autoneg) {
+		/* MLO_PAUSE_RX/TX are the manual override, consulted only
+		 * while pause AN is off, and they stay clear until something
+		 * writes them. While pause AN is on the request is carried by
+		 * the advertisement, so invert the mapping applied by
+		 * linkmode_set_pause(). Reporting the override bits instead
+		 * understates an advertised request, and the ethtool netlink
+		 * layer diffs a set against this reply and drops one that
+		 * matches, so such a request is lost without an error.
+		 */
+		rx = phylink_test(adv, Pause);
+		tx = rx ^ phylink_test(adv, Asym_Pause);
+	} else {
+		rx = pl->link_config.pause & MLO_PAUSE_RX;
+		tx = pl->link_config.pause & MLO_PAUSE_TX;
+	}
+
+	pause->rx_pause = rx;
+	pause->tx_pause = tx;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(phylink_ethtool_get_pauseparam);
 
